  "hypotheses": [
    "An agenda-by-agenda coverage checklist may reduce omitted discussions.",
    "A chronological transition sweep followed by an agenda reverse-check may recover more starts while preserving the evidence threshold and conditional item accuracy."
  ],
  "acceptance_signal_for_this_exploratory_screen": "More human item-and-boundary hits than same-run baseline, no reduction in conditional item accuracy, and no decrease in valid packet count.",
  "arms": {
    "baseline": "Current chapter-locator prompt, captured in the same run.",
    "agenda_checklist": "Coverage audit: work through agenda_items one at a time as a checklist, using agenda order only to ensure none are skipped. For each item, scan the entire transcript_units list for its spoken number or ID, title, locator cues, and semantically matching discussion. Find the first unit where substantive discussion begins; an item number does not have to be spoken if the discussion is otherwise clearly identifiable. Do not stop after finding several anchors or limit the answer to only the most prominent items. Before returning, check every agenda item again and include each one with clear, distinct transcript evidence. Keep the existing evidence bar: omit items whose discussion or start cannot be supported; do not guess. Preserve one anchor per agenda item and one use per unit, exact supplied IDs, and the required JSON schema.",
    "transition_sweep": "Coverage audit: first scan transcript_units chronologically from beginning to end and identify each clear transition into a new substantive topic or agenda discussion, including explicit announcements, motions, hearings, and clearly signaled topic changes. Then map each transition to the single best-supported agenda_item_index using the provided title, locator cues, and evidence_text. A mere speaker change or incidental mention is not a transition. After that pass, check the agenda list for any clearly discussed item you may have missed. Return all distinct, well-supported starts, not just the strongest few; omit uncertain matches rather than lowering the evidence bar. Preserve the exact JSON schema and the one-anchor-per-item / one-use-per-unit constraints."
  },
  "protocol": {
    "same_inputs_per_model": true,
    "arm_order": "Rotated by packet to balance order effects.",
    "requests_per_model": 24,
    "models": [
      "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
